# Introduction ^intro

!slide Why graphical models?

Many inference problems factorize. Instead of computing with a joint
distribution $p(x_1, \dots, x_n)$ directly, we exploit **structure**:

- global function = product of local factors
- inference = local computation + __message passing__
+ this is exactly the setting where asynchronous, distributed algorithms shine

